{"id":"c87c38e8cb3648339fdcede6e415b50a4d7d03c0","axis":"silent","repo":"vimeo/psalm","sha":"c87c38e8cb3648339fdcede6e415b50a4d7d03c0","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/annotating_code/library_authors.md","lines":["@@ -131,7 +131,7 @@ See [`@method`, `@psalm-property` and `@mixin`](supported_annotations.md)."," "," Psalm reads these tags as the `@psalm-*` equivalents, so a library that already annotates for PHPStan needs no second set:"," ","-`@phpstan-param`, `@phpstan-return`, `@phpstan-var`, `@phpstan-template`, `@phpstan-template-covariant`, `@phpstan-extends`, `@phpstan-implements`, `@phpstan-assert`, `@phpstan-assert-if-true`, `@phpstan-assert-if-false`, `@phpstan-param-out`, `@phpstan-pure`, `@phpstan-type`, `@phpstan-import-type`.","+`@phpstan-param`, `@phpstan-return`, `@phpstan-var`, `@phpstan-template`, `@phpstan-template-covariant`, `@phpstan-template-contravariant`, `@phpstan-extends`, `@phpstan-implements`, `@phpstan-assert`, `@phpstan-assert-if-true`, `@phpstan-assert-if-false`, `@phpstan-param-out`, `@phpstan-pure`, `@phpstan-type`, `@phpstan-import-type`."," "," [Supported annotations](supported_annotations.md) names a few more (`@phpstan-this-out`, `@phpstan-self-out`, `@phpstan-param-closure-this`, `@phpstan-require-extends`, `@phpstan-require-implements`)."," "],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/annotating_code/templated_annotations.md","lines":["@@ -1,302 +1,291 @@"," # Templating"," ","-Docblocks allow you to tell Psalm some simple information about how your code works. For example `@return int` in a function return type tells Psalm that a function should return an `int` and `@return MyContainer` tells Psalm that a function should return an instance of a user-defined class `MyContainer`. In either case, Psalm can check that the function actually returns those types _and_ that anything calling that function uses its returned value properly.","-","-Templated types allow you to tell Psalm even more information about how your code works.","-","-Let's look at a simple class `MyContainer`:","+A template is a placeholder for a type. A class or function declares it with `@template`, and Psalm replaces it with a real type wherever that class or function is used."," "," ```php"," <?php","-class MyContainer {","-  private $value;","-","-  public function __construct($value) {","-    $this->value = $value;","-  }","-","-  public function getValue() {","-    return $this->value;","-  }","+final class User {","+    public function __construct(public readonly string $name) {}"," }","-```"," ","-When Psalm handles the return type of `$my_container->getValue()` it doesn't know what it's getting out, because the value can be arbitrary.","-","-Templated annotations provide us with a workaround - we can define a generic/templated param `T` that is a placeholder for the value inside `MyContainer`:","-","-```php","-<?php","-/**","- * @template T","- */","-class MyContainer {","-  /** @var T */","-  private $value;","-","-  /** @param T $value */","-  public function __construct($value) {","-    $this->value = $value;","-  }","+/** @template T */","+final class Box {","+    /** @param T $value */","+    public function __construct(private readonly mixed $value) {}"," ","-  /** @return T */","-  public function getValue() {","-    return $this->value;","-  }","+    /** @return T */","+    public function get(): mixed {","+        return $this->value;","+    }"," }","-```","-","-Now we can substitute values for that templated param when we reference `MyContainer` in docblocks e.g. `@return MyContainer<int>`. This tells Psalm to substitute `T` for `int` when evaluating that return type, effectively treating it as a class that looks like"," ","-```php","-<?php","-class One_off_instance_of_MyContainer {","-  /** @var int */","-  private $value;","-","-  /** @param int $value */","-  public function __construct($value) {","-    $this->value = $value;","-  }","+/** @param Box<User> $box */","+function name(Box $box): string {","+    $user = $box->get(); // User","+    return $user->name;","+}"," ","-  /** @return int */","-  public function getValue() {","-    return $this->value;","-  }","+function f(User $user, string $name): void {","+    $box = new Box($user); // Box<User>","+    name($box); // no issue","+    name(new Box($name)); // InvalidArgument"," }"," ```"," ","-This pattern can be used in a large number of different situations like mocking, collections, iterators and loading arbitrary objects. Psalm has a large number of annotations to make it easy to use templated types in your codebase.","+In `Box<User>`, `T` is `User`, so `get()` returns a `User`. `new Box($user)` infers `T` from the constructor argument. Without the template, `get()` returns `mixed`."," "," ## `@template`, `@psalm-template`"," ","-The `@template`/`@psalm-template` tag allows classes and functions to declare a generic type parameter.","-","-As a very simple example, this function returns whatever is passed in:","+`@template` on a function or method declares a template that Psalm infers from the arguments of each call. Psalm reads `@psalm-template` and `@phpstan-template` the same way."," "," ```php"," <?php","+final class User {}","+"," /**","  * @template T","- * @psalm-param T $t","- * @return T","+ * @param list<T> $items","+ * @return T|null","  */","-function mirror($t) {","-    return $t;","+function first(array $items): mixed {","+    return $items[0] ?? null;"," }"," ","-$a = 5;","-$b = mirror($a); // Psalm knows the result is an int","-","-$c = \"foo\";","-$d = mirror($c); // Psalm knows the result is string","+/**","+ * @param list<User> $users","+ * @param list<int> $ids","+ */","+function f(array $users, array $ids): void {","+    $user = first($users); // User|null","+    $id = first($ids); // int|null","+}"," ```"," ","-Psalm also uses `@template` annotations in its stubbed versions of PHP array functions e.g.","+`@template` on a class, interface or trait declares a template of its objects. The type arguments follow the order of the `@template` tags: in `Collection<string, User>`, `TKey` is `string` and `TValue` is `User`. Psalm reports [MissingTemplateParam](../running_psalm/issues/MissingTemplateParam.md) if a type argument is missing."," "," ```php"," <?php","+final class User {","+    public function __construct(public readonly string $name) {}","+}","+"," /**","- * Takes one array with keys and another with values and combines them","- *","- * @template TKey","+ * @template TKey of array-key","  * @template TValue","- *","- * @param array<mixed, TKey> $arr","- * @param array<mixed, TValue> $arr2","- * @return array<TKey, TValue>","  */","-function array_combine(array $arr, array $arr2) {}","+final class Collection {","+    /** @param array<TKey, TValue> $items */","+    public function __construct(private readonly array $items) {}","+","+    /**","+     * @param TKey $key","+     * @return TValue|null","+     */","+    public function get(int|string $key): mixed {","+        return $this->items[$key] ?? null;","+    }","+","+    /**","+     * @template TNew","+     * @param callable(TValue): TNew $callback","+     * @return Collection<TKey, TNew>","+     */","+    public function map(callable $callback): Collection {","+        return new Collection(array_map($callback, $this->items));","+    }","+}","+","+/** @param Collection<string, User> $users */","+function f(Collection $users): void {","+    $user = $users->get('ann'); // User|null","+    $names = $users->map(fn(User $user): string => $user->name); // Collection<string, string>","+}","+","+/** @param Collection<string> $users */ // MissingTemplateParam","+function g(Collection $users): void {}"," ```"," ","-### Notes","-- `@template` tag order matters for class docblocks, as they dictate the order in which those generic parameters are referenced in docblocks.","-- The names of your templated types (e.g. `TKey`, `TValue`) don't matter outside the scope of the class or function in which they're declared.","+`TKey of array-key` is a [template constraint](#template-constraints). A template name is only known inside the class or function that declares it."," "," ## @param class-string&lt;T&gt;"," ","-Psalm also allows you to parameterize class types","+A `class-string<T>` parameter infers `T` from the class name that is passed."," "," ```php"," <?php","-/**","- * @template T of Foo","- * @psalm-param class-string<T> $class","- * @return T","- */","-function instantiator(string $class) {","-    return new $class();","-}","+interface Logger {}","+final class FileLogger implements Logger {}"," ","-class Foo {","-    public final function __construct() {}","+interface Container {","+    /**","+     * @template T","+     * @param class-string<T> $id","+     * @return T","+     */","+    public function get(string $id): object;"," }"," ","-class FooChild extends Foo {}","-","-$r = instantiator(FooChild::class);","-// Psalm knows $r is an object of type FooChild","+function f(Container $container, string $name): void {","+    $logger = $container->get(FileLogger::class); // FileLogger","+    $logger = $container->get(Logger::class); // Logger","+    $container->get($name); // ArgumentTypeCoercion","+}"," ```"," "," ## Template inheritance"," ","-Psalm allows you to extend templated classes with `@extends`/`@template-extends`:","+A class that extends a templated class gives the type arguments of its parent with `@extends` (or `@template-extends`). An argument can be a template of the child (`TypedList` below). Without the tag, Psalm reports [MissingTemplateParam](../running_psalm/issues/MissingTemplateParam.md) and each template of the parent stands for its constraint."," "," ```php"," <?php","-/**","- * @template T","- */","-class ParentClass {}","+final class User {}"," "," /**","- * @extends ParentClass<int>","+ * @template TKey of array-key","+ * @template TValue","  */","-class ChildClass extends ParentClass {}","-```","+class Collection {","+    /** @param array<TKey, TValue> $items */","+    public function __construct(protected array $items = []) {}","+","+    /**","+     * @param TKey $key","+     * @return TValue|null","+     */","+    public function get(int|string $key): mixed {","+        return $this->items[$key] ?? null;","+    }","+}"," ","-similarly you can implement interfaces with `@implements`/`@template-implements`","+/** @extends Collection<int, User> */","+final class UserCollection extends Collection {}"," ","-```php","-<?php"," /**","  * @template T","+ * @extends Collection<int, T>","  */","-interface IFoo {}","+final class TypedList extends Collection {}"," ","-/**","- * @implements IFoo<int>","- */","-class Foo implements IFoo {}","+final class Tags extends Collection {} // MissingTemplateParam","+","+$users = new UserCollection([new User()]);","+$user = $users->get(0); // User|null","+$users->get('ann'); // InvalidArgument","+new UserCollection(['Ann']); // InvalidArgument","+","+$list = new TypedList([new User()]); // TypedList<User>","+$user = $list->get(0); // User|null"," ```"," ","-and import traits with `@use`/`@template-use`","+`@implements` (or `@template-implements`) does the same for an interface, and `@use` (or `@template-use`) for a trait. The `@use` docblock goes on the `use` statement."," "," ```php"," <?php","-/**","- * @template T","- */","-trait MyTrait {}","+final class User {}"," ","-class Foo {","-    /**","-     * @use MyTrait<int>","-     */","-    use MyTrait;","+/** @template T of object */","+interface Repository {","+    /** @return T|null */","+    public function find(int $id): ?object;"," }","-```"," ","-You can also extend one templated class with another, e.g.","+/** @template T of object */","+trait StoresInMemory {","+    /** @var array<int, T> */","+    private array $rows = [];"," ","-```php","-<?php","-/**","- * @template T1","- */","-class ParentClass {}","+    /** @return T|null */","+    public function find(int $id): ?object {","+        return $this->rows[$id] ?? null;","+    }"," ","-/**","- * @template T2","- * @extends ParentClass<T2>","- */","-class ChildClass extends ParentClass {}","+    /** @param T $row */","+    public function save(int $id, object $row): void {","+        $this->rows[$id] = $row;","+    }","+}","+","+/** @implements Repository<User> */","+final class UserRepository implements Repository {","+    /** @use StoresInMemory<User> */","+    use StoresInMemory;","+}","+","+$users = new UserRepository();","+$user = $users->find(1); // User|null","+$users->save(1, new User()); // no issue","+$users->save(2, new DateTime()); // InvalidArgument"," ```"," "," ## Template constraints"," ","-You can use `@template of <type>` to restrict input. For example, to restrict to a given class you can use","+`@template T of Type` only allows `Type` and its subtypes for `T`. Inside the function or class, a `T` value can be used as a `Type`. A template without a constraint allows any type."," "," ```php"," <?php","-class Foo {}","-class FooChild extends Foo {}","+abstract class Model {","+    public int $id = 0;","+}","+final class User extends Model {}"," "," /**","- * @template T of Foo","- * @psalm-param T $t","- * @return array<int, T>","+ * @template T of Model","+ * @param T $model","+ * @return T","  */","-function makeArray($t) {","-    return [$t];","+function save(Model $model): Model {","+    echo $model->id; // no issue","+    return $model;"," }","-$a = makeArray(new Foo()); // typed as array<int, Foo>","-$b = makeArray(new FooChild()); // typed as array<int, FooChild>","-$c = makeArray(new stdClass()); // type error","+","+$user = save(new User()); // User","+save(new DateTime()); // InvalidArgument","+","+/** @template T of Model */","+interface Repository {}","+","+/** @param Repository<DateTime> $dates */ // InvalidTemplateParam","+function f(Repository $dates): void {}"," ```"," ","-Templated types aren't limited to key-value pairs, and you can re-use templates across multiple arguments of a template-supporting type:","+A templated class written without type arguments stands for its constraints: `Repository` is `Repository<Model>`, and a `Repository<User>` is not a `Repository<Model>` (see [Template covariance](#template-covariance)). Only a template without a constraint accepts every type argument there. To accept every `Repository`, use a [star projection](#star-projection).","+"," ```php"," <?php","-/**","- * @template T0 of array-key","- *","- * @template-implements IteratorAggregate<T0, int>","- */","-abstract class Foo implements IteratorAggregate {","-  /**","-   * @var int","-   */","-  protected $rand_min;","-","-  /**","-   * @var int","-   */","-  protected $rand_max;","-","-  public function __construct(int $rand_min, int $rand_max) {","-    $this->rand_min = $rand_min;","-    $this->rand_max = $rand_max;","-  }","-","-  /**","-   * @return Generator<T0, int, mixed, T0>","-   */","-  public function getIterator() : Generator {","-    $j = random_int($this->rand_min, $this->rand_max);","-    for($i = $this->rand_min; $i <= $j; $i += 1) {","-      yield $this->getFuzzyType($i) => $i ** $i;","-    }","+abstract class Model {}","+final class User extends Model {}"," ","-    return $this->getFuzzyType($j);","-  }","-","-  /**","-   * @return T0","-   */","-  abstract protected function getFuzzyType(int $i);","+/** @template T of Model */","+interface Repository {","+    /** @return T|null */","+    public function find(int $id): ?Model;"," }"," ","-/**","- * @template-extends Foo<int>","- */","-class Bar extends Foo {","-  protected function getFuzzyType(int $i) : int {","-    return $i;","-  }","+function takesBare(Repository $repository): void {","+    $model = $repository->find(1); // Model|null"," }"," ","-/**","- * @template-extends Foo<string>","- */","-class Baz extends Foo {","-  protected function getFuzzyType(int $i) : string {","-    return static::class . '[' . $i . ']';","-  }","+/** @param Repository<*> $repository */","+function takesAny(Repository $repository): void {}","+","+/** @param Repository<User> $users */","+function f(Repository $users): void {","+    takesBare($users); // InvalidArgument","+    takesAny($users); // no issue"," }"," ```"," "," ## Template defaults"," ","-A template can have a default type, written after `=`: `@template T = Default`, or `@template T of Bound = Default` with a bound. `@template-covariant` and the `@psalm-template` and `@phpstan-template` forms take one the same way.","+`@template T = Default` gives a template a default type. A constraint comes before it: `@template T of Constraint = Default`. `@template-covariant`, `@template-contravariant`, `@psalm-template` and `@phpstan-template` take a default the same way."," ","-Psalm uses the default when the type argument is left out:","+Psalm uses the default where the type argument is left out:"," ","-* in `@extends`, `@implements` and `@use` that leave out trailing templates, if each of them has a default;","-* when a class is extended, implemented or used without one of those tags (templates without a default get their bound);","-* in a generic type with only its first arguments given, such as `Result<string>` in a `@param`, `@return`, `@var` or property type;","-* in `new`, for templates the constructor arguments don't infer. If the class has a constructor and one of its own public methods or properties (not an inherited, trait, `@method` or `@property` one) takes the template, `new` leaves it to later code in the function instead, and it stands for its bound if that code never fixes it;","-* in a function or method call, for templates the arguments don't infer.","+* in a generic type that gives only the first type arguments, such as `Result<string>` in a `@param`, `@return`, `@var` or property type;","+* in `@extends`, `@implements` and `@use` that leave out trailing templates;","+* in a class that extends, implements or uses a templated one without that tag. A template without a default gets its constraint there, and Psalm reports [MissingTemplateParam](../running_psalm/issues/MissingTemplateParam.md);","+* in `new`, for a template that the constructor arguments don't infer;","+* in a function or method call, for a template that the arguments don't infer."," "," ```php"," <?php","@@ -305,28 +294,62 @@ Psalm uses the default when the type argument is left out:","  * @template TError of Throwable = RuntimeException","  */"," class Result {","-    /** @var TError|null */","-    public ?Throwable $error = null;","+    /**","+     * @param TValue $value","+     * @param TError|null $error","+     */","+    public function __construct(","+        public readonly mixed $value = null,","+        public readonly ?Throwable $error = null,","+    ) {}"," }"," "," /** @extends Result<int> */"," final class IntResult extends Result {}","-final class VoidResult extends Result {}"," ","-$result = new Result(); // Result<null, RuntimeException>","-$error = (new IntResult())->error; // RuntimeException|null","-$error = (new VoidResult())->error; // RuntimeException|null","+final class EmptyResult extends Result {}"," "," /** @param Result<string> $partial */","-function check(Result $partial, Result $bare): void {","-    $error = $partial->error; // RuntimeException|null","-    $error = $bare->error; // Throwable|null","+function f(Result $partial, IntResult $int, EmptyResult $empty, Result $bare): void {","+    $partial->error; // RuntimeException|null","+    $int->error; // RuntimeException|null","+    $empty->value; // null","+    $empty->error; // RuntimeException|null","+    $bare->error; // Throwable|null"," }","+","+$result = new Result(); // Result<null, RuntimeException>","+$result = new Result(null, new LogicException()); // Result<null, LogicException>"," ```"," ","-Defaults don't apply to a class name without type arguments (PHPStan applies them there). `Result` alone still stands for its bounds, compared with the usual variance rules: `TError` is `Throwable`, and `TValue`, bounded by `mixed`, stays open, as does a template bounded by a set of capabilities. Templates without a default are unaffected.","+A class name without type arguments does not use the defaults (PHPStan uses them there). `Result` alone stands for [its constraints](#template-constraints), so `$bare->error` is `Throwable|null`.","+","+For an invariant or covariant template, `new` does not use the default if a public method parameter or a public writable property takes the template. The class must declare that method or property itself: inherited, trait, `@method` and `@property` members don't count. Later code in the function can still fix such a template (see [Type variables](type_variables.md)). If no code does, the template stands for its constraint. `new` never leaves a [contravariant](#template-contravariance) template to later code.","+","+```php","+<?php","+/** @template T = int */","+final class Queue {","+    /** @param T $item */","+    public function push(mixed $item): void {}","+}","+","+/** @return Queue<string> */","+function names(): Queue {","+    $queue = new Queue();","+    $queue->push('Ann');","+    return $queue; // no issue","+}"," ","-Method templates take defaults too, and a default can use the templates of its class:","+/** @return Queue<string> */","+function ids(): Queue {","+    $queue = new Queue();","+    $queue->push(1); // IncompatibleTypeParameters","+    return $queue;","+}","+```","+","+A method template takes a default too, and the default can use the templates of the class:"," "," ```php"," <?php","@@ -341,13 +364,16 @@ interface Option {"," }"," "," /** @param Option<int> $option */","-function check(Option $option): void {","+function f(Option $option): void {","     $same = $option->map(); // Option<int>","     $mapped = $option->map(fn(int $i): bool => $i > 0); // Option<bool>"," }"," ```"," ","-A call still infers a template from its arguments and parameter defaults where it can. A `null` for `T|null` infers `null` if the bound admits it, and an argument that doesn't say what `T` is (a bare `Setting` for `Setting<T>`, a bare `callable` for `callable(): T`) infers the bound, not the default:","+In a call, an argument that fixes the template wins over the default. Two cases are less obvious:","+","+* `null` for a `T|null` parameter, passed or left to the parameter default, infers `null` if the constraint allows `null`. Otherwise Psalm uses the default.","+* An argument that does not say what `T` is, such as a `Setting` without type arguments for a `Setting<T>` parameter, infers the constraint, not the default."," "," ```php"," <?php","@@ -377,250 +403,388 @@ interface Timeouts {","     public function configured(Setting $setting): int;"," }"," ","-function check(Timeouts $timeouts, Setting $setting): void {","+/** @param Setting<5> $five */","+function f(Timeouts $timeouts, Setting $bare, Setting $five): void {","+    $seconds = $timeouts->connect(10); // 10","     $seconds = $timeouts->connect(); // 30","     $seconds = $timeouts->connect(null); // 30","     $seconds = $timeouts->idle(); // null","     $seconds = $timeouts->idle(null); // null","-    $seconds = $timeouts->configured($setting); // int"],"additions":539,"deletions":347,"truncated":true},{"path":"psalm-baseline.xml","lines":["@@ -225,10 +225,8 @@","       <code><![CDATA[$context->self]]></code>","       <code><![CDATA[$parent_storage->template_types]]></code>","       <code><![CDATA[$resolved_name]]></code>","-      <code><![CDATA[$storage->template_covariants]]></code>","       <code><![CDATA[$storage->template_extended_params]]></code>","       <code><![CDATA[$storage->template_types]]></code>","-      <code><![CDATA[$storage->template_types]]></code>","     </RiskyTruthyFalsyComparison>","   </file>","   <file src=\"src/Psalm/Internal/Analyzer/ClosureAnalyzer.php\">","@@ -2866,6 +2864,7 @@","                 $this,","                 $container_type_params_covariant,","                 $input_star_offse